# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#  DENY-BY-DEFAULT for binaries.
#
#  A committed binary lives in git history forever — removing it
#  needs git filter-repo, a force-push, and everyone re-cloning.
#  So: block every binary format, then allow back only what we
#  authored ourselves.
#
#  Governing rule: COMMIT WHAT WE AUTHORED.
#  Raw source material gets a SOURCES.md manifest, never a blob.
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# ── Documents & archives ───────────────────────────────────────
*.pdf
*.ppt
*.pptx
*.pot
*.potx
*.doc
*.docx
*.xls
*.xlsx
*.odt
*.odp
*.ods
*.zip
*.7z
*.rar
*.tar
*.gz

# ── Installers & disk images ───────────────────────────────────
# (the 10 GB ANSYS Electronics zip is caught by *.zip above)
*.iso
*.exe
*.msi
*.dmg
*.appimage

# ── Media ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.jpg
*.jpeg
*.png
*.gif
*.tif
*.tiff
*.bmp
*.webp
*.mp4
*.mov
*.avi
*.mp3
*.wav

# ── Allow back: material we authored ───────────────────────────
# SVG is text — it diffs properly and our figures are redrawn by hand.
!**/figures/*.svg
!docs/img/*.svg

# Past-paper scans are NOT committed. This repository is public, and a scan is a
# verbatim photographic reproduction of a university examination paper — the
# university's copyright, not ours. Keep scans locally if you want them; the
# transcription in past-papers/*.md is what gets shared.
#
# (No negation here on purpose. The media rules above already ignore them.)

# ── Source material — lecturer / publisher copyright ───────────
# Never committed. Each subject's SOURCES.md says what belongs here.
# NOTE: single * (not **) so the negations below still work —
# git cannot re-include a file whose parent directory is excluded.
**/sources/*
!**/sources/SOURCES.md
!**/sources/.gitkeep

# ── Page-by-page transcripts — the extraction working layer ────
# Ours in the sense that we typed them, but ~95% of each file IS the
# lecturer's page, transcribed line for line. That is the same thing
# sources/ holds, so it gets the same treatment: kept locally, never
# committed. The knowledge base beside it is the authored product —
# reorganised, corrected and analysed — and that is what ships.
# Each subject's SOURCES.md says these exist and what they are for.
**/knowledge-base/_transcripts/

# ── Third-party lab material — copyright ───────────────────────
# BEE 3102's laboratory material reproduces a published commercial lab
# manual's procedure text verbatim and keeps crops of its pages. That
# breaks docs/kb-format.md § "What never gets committed", rule 3, and the
# commit-what-we-authored principle.
#
# These rules previously lived in .git/info/exclude, which is LOCAL ONLY —
# it does not survive a clone, so a fresh checkout elsewhere would have
# nothing stopping it publishing the crops. Moved here so the protection
# travels with the repository.
#
# To publish: paraphrase the procedure text and discussion questions,
# delete labs/figures/scan/, then remove the two lines below.
digital-electronics/knowledge-base/labs/
digital-electronics/study-guides/lab-01-ttl-nand-nor.html

# ── Personal overlay — never shared ────────────────────────────
_personal/
_Study Log/
**/*.private.md

# ── Quarantine & build artifacts ───────────────────────────────
_to_delete/
build/
dist/
*.tmp

# ── Python bytecode from the lab/assignment scripts ────────────
# The .py files ARE committed; their compiled output never is.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# ── Subjects without a knowledge base yet ──────────────────────
# (none — Thermodynamics now has one. Its raw material is covered by the
#  **/sources/* rule above, plus the *.pdf / *.docx / *.zip extension rules.
#  Do NOT re-add a blanket `thermodynamics/` line: core.ignorecase is true on
#  Windows, so it would also swallow thermodynamics/knowledge-base/.)

# ── Windows / OneDrive / Office ────────────────────────────────
desktop.ini
Thumbs.db
ehthumbs.db
$RECYCLE.BIN/
~$*
*.lnk
.~lock.*

# ── macOS (classmates on Mac) ──────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes

# ── Editors ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*~
